From 98b1a2f10fed7f88ef7f7433098f0680312deba4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:40:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(test): six refusal suites take the oblique not-judged
 device

#2182 (#2177) made the program sim judge a stock box turned a quarter
about Z. Six suites (circular_pick_law, trochoid_law, keep_law,
kept_parts_live, stock_source_holes, pocket3d_open_side) still used
that turn to make the sim refuse. Their checks that the operation's own
clause holds the post saw the sim's gouge clause first, and 18 tests
went red on main. The post stayed refused in 17 of them.

The suites now turn the stock 1e-6 rad about Z, the #2177 device, and
each such check also asserts that the sim refuses the stock by name.
No never-posts assert is removed. The 18th case (an added-part chamfer
that posts where the sim judges) is a code defect, filed as #2308.

Fixes #2306

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
